   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1941-02-20">February <hi rend="hand"><hi rend="above"
                           >th</hi></hi> 1941.</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__605" type="person">Mr. Raymond B. Fosdick</rs><lb/> The
               Rockefeller Foundation<lb/> 49 West 49th Street<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__605" type="person">Mr.
                  Fosdick</rs>,</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>You have, I suppose, received the letter of my colleague, <rs
                  ref="#tillich_person_id__4199" type="person">Dr. Harry Emerson Fosdick</rs>,
               concerning the project of the International Institute of Social Research at Colombia
               University.</p>
            <p>Since, for the reasons given in my letter<note type="ea">liegt nicht vor</note> to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4199" type="person">Dr. Fosdick</rs>,
            this project is very close to my heart and there may be some points which could be clarified
            by a personal conversation, I should like very much to speak to you about the whole problem
            at a time convenient to you.</p><closer>
               <salute>Very sincerely yours,</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person"
                  >Paul Tillich</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
